{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmSlit","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.ParametricIntervalIntegral"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.analyticOnNhd_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.analyticOnNhd_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L243-L250","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt` is analytic on `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`.**\n\nThis is the statement `qou-clx8` set out to prove: the integral definition really\n*is* the analytic continuation, not merely a function agreeing with the series on\nthe disc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.differentiableOn_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.differentiableOn_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L239-L241","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt` is differentiable on `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt'","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L204-L237","doc":"The closed form, for `w ≠ 0`: `d/dw Li₂(w) = −log(1−w)/w`.\n\n`∫₀¹ (1 − wz)⁻¹ dz = −log(1−w)/w` by the fundamental theorem of calculus, the\nantiderivative in `z` being `−log(1 − wz)/w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L144-L202","doc":"**`cLiTwoExt` is complex-differentiable off the cut**, with derivative given\nby the integral of the differentiated integrand.\n\nThe value is stated as an integral rather than in closed form on purpose — see\nthe module docstring: `-(log (1−w)/w)` is Lean-junk `0` at `w = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_integrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_integrand","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L130-L142","doc":"The `w`-derivative of the integrand, pointwise in `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.exists_uniform_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.exists_uniform_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L90-L126","doc":"**`‖1 − w·z‖` is bounded below, uniformly for `w` near `w₀` and `z ∈ [0,1]`.**\n\nThis is the hypothesis `hasDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_deriv_le` needs\nand the only real work in this file: with it the dominating function is a\nconstant.\n\nCompactness, not estimates. `ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` is open, so some closed ball around `w₀`\nstays inside it; on that ball `mem_slitPlane_one_sub_mul` puts `1 − wz` in\n`slitPlane`, which excludes `0`; and a continuous, nowhere-zero function on the\ncompact `closedBall ×ˢ Icc 0 1` attains a positive minimum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_notCut_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_notCut_iff","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isOpen_notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isOpen_notCut","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L75-L83","doc":"**`ℂ ∖ [1,∞)` is open.** Its complement `{w | w.im = 0 ∧ 1 ≤ w.re}` is the\nintersection of two closed preimages. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.notCut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.notCut","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmDeriv.lean#L72-L73","doc":"The complement of the cut, as a predicate: `w.im ≠ 0 ∨ w.re < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}